{{!-- A1, "editorial rows", on Recommendations: a row per publication.

	{{> "directory/rec-rows"}}      from partials/recommendations.hbs, in the helper's context

BOTH ACTIONS REACH A REAL DESTINATION. In the reference build they are inert, because there is
nothing on the other end of a fictional publication; here "Visit" is the recommendation's own URL
and "Subscribe" is that publication's Portal signup.

`#/portal/signup` is a safe suffix precisely where `one_click_subscribe` is true: Ghost sets that
flag by asking the recommended URL whether it is a Ghost site with members enabled, so the button
only appears where a Portal exists to open.

WHAT ONE-CLICK SUBSCRIBE ACTUALLY IS, AND WHY THIS IS NOT IT. Inside Portal's own recommendation
modal a signed-in Member subscribes to a recommended publication without leaving the page —
Portal holds the member's email and posts it for them. That flow lives in Portal's React bundle
and a theme has no way to invoke it, so the button here opens the other publication's signup
instead, with the reader's email still to type. Recorded as a Concession in DECISIONS.md.

`data-recommendation="{{id}}"` is what makes the click count: Portal binds a listener to every
`[data-recommendation]` element on the page and posts to
`/members/api/recommendations/{id}/clicked/` (`setupRecommendationButtons` in portal 2.71,
`core/server/web/members/app.js` for the endpoint). Without the attribute the publication's own
recommendation stats stay at zero and nothing else breaks — which is exactly the kind of silent
loss worth a comment.

`target="_blank" rel="noopener"` matches Ghost's own template: a recommendation points off the
publication, and the reader is mid-visit here.

`{{this.url}}` AND NOT `{{url}}`. `url` is a registered Ghost helper, and Handlebars resolves a
bare mustache as a helper before it looks at the context — so `{{url}}` here returns the URL of
the page being rendered, and every recommendation linked to `/`. It cost a scored run to see,
because the row still looked right: the visible address is `{{readable_url url}}`, where `url` is
a helper ARGUMENT and therefore a plain path lookup, so the text said `marginalpress.com` while
the href said `/`. `this.` forces the context lookup. --}}
<section
	id="recs"
	aria-label="{{t "Recommended publications"}}"
	style="--container-max:1120px"
	class="border-border container border-t">
	{{#foreach recommendations}}
		<article
			class="border-border max-stack:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] max-stack:gap-5 grid grid-cols-[44px_minmax(0,1fr)_auto] items-start gap-7 border-b py-[34px]">
			{{#if favicon}}
				<img
					src="{{img_url favicon size="xs"}}"
					alt=""
					width="44"
					height="44"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
					class="border-border block h-11 w-11 rounded-sm border object-cover">
			{{else}}
				<span
					aria-hidden="true"
					class="border-border bg-surface-2 block h-11 w-11 rounded-sm border"></span>
			{{/if}}

			<div>
				<h2 class="font-display tracking-heading text-[28px] leading-[1.18] font-medium">
					<a
						href="{{this.url}}"
						data-recommendation="{{id}}"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener"
						class="text-text no-underline">{{title}}</a>
				</h2>

				<p class="text-muted mt-2 font-mono text-[11.5px]">{{readable_url url}}</p>

				{{#if description}}
					<p class="text-body text-muted mt-3 max-w-[60ch] leading-[1.62] text-pretty">{{description}}</p>
				{{/if}}
			</div>

			<div class="max-stack:items-start max-stack:flex-row max-stack:flex-wrap flex flex-col items-end gap-2">
				{{#if one_click_subscribe}}
					<a
						href="{{this.url}}#/portal/signup"
						data-recommendation="{{id}}"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener"
						class="btn btn-primary font-ui rounded-sm border px-[18px] py-2.5 text-[13.5px] font-semibold whitespace-nowrap no-underline">{{t "Subscribe"}}</a>
				{{/if}}

				<a
					href="{{this.url}}"
					data-recommendation="{{id}}"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener"
					class="border-border text-text font-ui rounded-sm border px-[18px] py-2.5 text-[13.5px] font-semibold whitespace-nowrap no-underline">{{t "Visit"}}
					{{!-- Archivo carries no arrow glyph; the design source falls through to system-ui, so
					it is pinned rather than left to the fallback chain. --}}
					<span class="font-[system-ui,sans-serif]">&rarr;</span></a>
			</div>
		</article>
	{{/foreach}}
</section>
